WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.280
Third grade. The fossil kit is open, and every table has a trilobite.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.590
Ms. Rivera: Look closely. What do you notice?

00:00:08.843 --> 00:00:10.553
Malik: It's a bug! A giant bug!

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:12.613
Pause. What would you say next?

00:00:17.164 --> 00:00:19.534
Ms. Rivera: What do you see that makes you say that?

00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:22.424
Malik: It has lots of legs. And all these little stripes.

00:00:22.474 --> 00:00:26.894
Asking for evidence keeps Malik looking, and the whole class looks closer.

00:00:28.144 --> 00:00:29.114
Sofía: Patas?

00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:32.514
Ms. Rivera: I see legs. Veo patas. Show your partner where.

00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:39.134
A sentence frame in both languages lets Sofia share what she noticed, and build English at the same time.

00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:48.898
Three moves for any object. Ask for evidence. Offer frames in students' languages. Turn disagreements into investigations.
